  "derived": {
    "samples": [
      {
        "label": "Total cigarette purchase by Region, Segment and Year",
        "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
        "updated": "2025-02-06T09:30:00Z",
        "note": [
          "Indicator definition: Number of cigarettes per inhabitant aged 15 and above. The total purchase is the sum of the unregistered cigarette purchase and the registered cigarette purchase. The unregistered purchase comprises cigarettes imported during travel abroad and the purchase of smuggled cigarettes. The registered purchase comprises sale of taxed cigarettes in Sweden. At the turn of the half-year of 2013, certain changes were made to the methods used in the Monitor Study. The age interval in the sample changed from 16-80 years to 17-84 years, however the changes have impacted the results to a small degree, which entails that the reported data is comparable over time. In 2003 the non-responde rate was 50% and thereafter it increased to 74% in 2016/17. Since then a decline has occurred and in 2021 the non-respons rate was 66 %."
        ],
